v 3
d 'SELDECOMP': raking-based reweighting decomposition of group differences in means
d
d  seldecomp decomposes the difference in the mean of an outcome
d between two groups into a part explained by group differences in
d the distributions of a set of categorical (or binned continuous)
d raking variables and an unexplained remainder, using the
d nonparametric raking (iterative proportional fitting) method of
d Pylypchuk and Selden (2008, Journal of Health Economics).
d
d KW: decomposition
d KW: Oaxaca-Blinder-Kitagawa
d KW: Oaxaca-Blinder
d KW: raking
d KW: reweighting
d KW: iterative proportional fitting
d KW: group differences
d KW: Bayesian bootstrap
d
d Requires: Stata version 16.1
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261118
d
d Author: Tom Selden & Thomas A. Hegland
d Support: email thomas.hegland@ahrq.hhs.gov
d
